      "notes": "NEXT-SESSION ACTIVITY (user-requested 2026-06-30). Goal: rigorously vet whether the dashboard surfaces MEANINGFUL, ACTIONABLE insight or just trivia — from a real end-user's perspective. The user's stated fear: 'the things it is surfacing are pretty trivial and meaningless.' Findings may indicate dashboard problems OR problems in the underlying metrics/insights themselves; capture both. Use the extensive critique as a baseline for improvement.\n\nSETUP: generate a fresh dashboard (graph dashboard --db .codewatch/graph.db --config .codewatch/check.json --repo codewatch --repo-root . --vs <~20-snapshots-back> --out <file>) AND generate for 1-2 FOREIGN repos (voltras-mcp, brain) so the critique isn't codewatch-incestuous. The 7 views: Overview, Hotspots, Architecture (Main sequence + Dependency graph tabs), Coupling, Ownership, Fitness, Drift.\n\nMETHOD: assign ONE async agent per view (7 agents). Each agent MUST: (1) render the view in a headless browser (playwright is a devDep in dashboard/), read the DOM (accessibility tree + text), and take fullPage screenshots at 1440x940 (and interact: click a node/row, open the Dossier, sort/filter); (2) critique AESTHETICS — general visual quality, spacing/padding/rhythm, typography/font choices, color usage, information density, visual hierarchy, alignment/grid, empty states, responsiveness; (3) critique CONTENT/ACTIONABILITY from an end user who does NOT know the project well: what are the action items implied by what I'm shown? Is it clear how to INTERPRET each number/widget? Does it help me understand the project if I'm new? If something is flagged as an error/violation, do I know what to DO about it, and is that thing ACTUALLY worth doing? Am I getting genuinely actionable insight, or restating trivia? Is the signal real or an artifact of the metric (e.g. bus-factor saturating at 100% on single-author repos, abstractness proxy being ~0, scary-hotspots just re-flagging big files)? For each finding, tag whether it's a DASHBOARD issue or an UNDERLYING METRIC/INSIGHT issue.\n\nOUTPUT: each agent returns a ranked findings list (aesthetics + content, CONFIRMED vs SUSPECTED, with screenshot refs). Then synthesize across all 7 into a single prioritized 'dashboard vetting' doc (active-work deepdive source) that becomes the improvement backlog. Expect this to spawn concrete follow-up tasks (both UI polish AND metric/insight rework). This is genuine vetting of the surface's VALUE, not just bug-finding — be skeptical and demanding; assume the insights are trivial until proven otherwise.",
