        "first_line": "# Flesh out the 9 stub initiatives",
        "body": "# Flesh out the 9 stub initiatives\n\nLast session created 13 initiatives via discover/fold but only 4 had real briefs (active-work, voltras-workspace, home-assistant, computer-organization). The other 9 were stubs (`Why: ...` / `_(write a paragraph here)_`).\n\nThis session: filled `brief.md` + `handoff.md` for all 9 — audiobook (template, written by hand), then brain / codewatch / denver-rezzy / health / logan / taxes / voltras-mcp / youtube via 8 parallel general-purpose subagents pointed at each source project.\n\n## Output\n\n- 13 initiatives parse cleanly; `active-work audit --json` reports no parse errors or worktree conflicts\n- Per-initiative line counts (brief / handoff): audiobook 44/23, brain 57/33, codewatch 48/33, denver-rezzy 64/31, health 38/18, logan 71/29, taxes 52/27, voltras-mcp 52/32, youtube 43/21\n- YAML frontmatter preserved byte-for-byte on every brief\n- Each brief follows the structure: Why this exists / Architecture (or Folder layout) / Sub-projects or Workstreams / Stakeholders / Open questions and risks / References\n- Each handoff: Current state / Open blockers or decisions / Next actions / Environmental items\n\n## Notable findings surfaced during the writeup\n\n- **brain**: `main` (`6da9d96`) ships VNM-56 worktree fixes; `spike/2026-05-platform` holds a 10-package Restate + Agent SDK rewrite proposal. Decision memo `07-spike-1-decision-memo.md` (2026-05-12) recommends adopting the spike stack but there's no migration plan. ~80 untracked docs in working tree.\n- **codewatch**: in-repo handoff at `docs/2026-05-12-codewatch-evening-merges-handoff.md` is the canonical re-entry doc. Branch `feat/lcom-metric @ 26c1093` has LCOM4 in flight. Internal `@code-style/*` package names lag the directory + remote rename.\n- **denver-rezzy**: NO `.git/` — reconstructed status from CLAUDE.md + `docs/HANDOFF.md` + file mtimes. Task 4 (platform listings backfill) likely in progress past the Apr 30 snapshot.\n- **audiobook**: local main 24 ahead of `origin/main`, which is 3 ahead of merge base. Working tree has uncommitted titan-design migration changes.\n- **voltras-mcp**: scoped to the MCP server slice; `[[voltras-workspace]]` covers cross-repo coordination. `agent/VMCP-02.06-04@12fe592` worktree still holds G's `device.unload` awaiting hardware re-validation.\n- **logan**: family home renovation hub for 5145 S Logan Dr. DBS outdoor kitchen contract signed 2.13.26, trenching underway, heater electrician breakout overdue. Large SketchUp/Revit files; email is source of truth.\n- **taxes**: 2025 tax-year working dir staged for CPA via SafeSend; CHECKLIST.md tracks remaining items (Computershare, payment receipts, CP503 resolution).\n- **youtube**: ~230-line `extract.py` — yt-dlp subtitle pull → cleaned Markdown at `out/<video-id>.md`; `--whisper` flag for `faster-whisper` fallback (not yet installed).\n- **health**: source dir empty. Brief explicitly notes it's an intended-but-undefined workstream — first decision is what \"health tracking\" should mean (passive ingest? journaling? integration layer? possible overlap with `workout-analytics`).\n\n## Process notes\n\n- Dispatched all 8 subagents in parallel from one tool turn (background). All completed cleanly between ~44s and ~154s. Total wall time dominated by the longest agent (brain, 153s).\n- Each agent received: source path, initiative path, audiobook brief+handoff as the structural template, hard constraints (don't touch frontmatter, don't run CLI, don't modify source), and asked for a one-sentence-per-file report.\n- The agent for `health` correctly resisted padding an empty source — brief and handoff are shorter than the rest and lead with \"decide what this means\" as the first next action.\n- No retries, no failures, no parse errors after the fact.\n\n## Untouched / out of scope\n\n- No tasks were added via CLI — handoffs list next actions in prose, but the per-task structured `tasks/*.yml` files are still empty for the 9 newly-fleshed initiatives. Adding those is the obvious follow-up if any of these initiatives gets focused for real work.\n- The 4 untracked discover hits that remain (the `~/Users/hjewkes` root sessions, the 6 `smoke-agent-submission-*` temp dirs, and the `workout-analytics/.worktrees/WA-04.01` worktree) were not triaged this session."
