        "first_line": "## What we did",
        "body": "## What we did\n\nBuilt `@hjewkes/active-work` v0.1.0 from scratch in a single session — design, planning, implementation, integration, dogfood. 34 commits, 32 PRs, all merged to main, all CI green.\n\n## Wave-by-wave outcomes\n\n- **Wave 0** (PR #1): Repo scaffold — package.json, tsconfig, tsup, vitest workspaces, eslint flat config, prettier, MIT, GitHub Actions CI/release, branch protection.\n- **Wave 1** (PRs #2-6 + finalizer #17): 5 parallel agents shipped the primitive layer — zod schemas, fs-atomic + flock, gray-matter/YAML I/O, errors with sysexits, command registry types, vitest fixtures. Finalizer wired the registry into `src/commands/index.ts` and added `coerceDates` to fix a YAML 1.2 timestamp issue 5 agents had each worked around independently.\n- **Wave 2** (PRs #7-16): 10 parallel agents shipped 34 domain commands — lifecycle (new/set/touch/paths/rename/archive), focus/pause, tasks (add/done/list/edit/reorder/delete), sessions (record/list), source-add + artifact tracking, worktree.set-default + audit + list, discover/fold/drop/track + 4 discover sources, open + bootstrap prompt assembly, edit + sessions browser, lint module.\n- **Wave 3** (PRs #19-21): 3 parallel agents shipped the interfaces — commander dispatcher with --json envelope and usage log, stdio MCP server with tools auto-derived from the registry (using Zod 4's native `z.toJSONSchema` after the agent caught that `zod-to-json-schema` only supports v3), schema-version migration runner.\n- **Wave 4** (PR #23): First attempt stalled at 600s tangled on WebSocket-on-hono. Cut scope to ship the slim daemon: hono HTTP, MCP-over-HTTP via `StreamableHTTPServerTransport` (dispatched at the Node http.Server level to avoid hono's `ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT`), lifecycle commands, pino logging. Deferred WS and launchd to AW-3 / AW-2.\n- **Wave 5** (PRs #26-27): 2 parallel agents shipped dashboard (React + vite-singlefile, 203KB → 64KB gzipped) and skill content + postinstall.js. Dashboard agent dropped @titan-design/react-ui as overhead-without-benefit at v0; flagged as AW-11.\n- **Wave 6** (PR #29): 8-step interactive setup wizard + uninstall + changesets pipeline + initial 0.1.0 changeset. Mid-task an unsafe test deleted `~/.claude/skills/active-work/` — fixed with `vi.spyOn(os, 'homedir')`; manually restored the skill from main's `skill/` source.\n- **Wave 7** (PRs #30-32): 3 parallel agents shipped end-to-end + discover-orchestrator + daemon-roundtrip integration tests, full README + architecture.md + auto-generated cli-reference.md, and the dogfood scaffold at `dogfood/active-work/`.\n\n## Final stats\n\n- 48 test files, 429 tests passing\n- `dist/cli.js`: 154KB\n- `dist/dashboard/index.html`: 203KB (64KB gzipped)\n- 36 commands registered\n- Build clean, lint clean, typecheck clean\n\n## What's left\n\nSee AW-1 through AW-14. Top priorities: AW-13 (first npm publish), AW-9 (test-safety audit), AW-1 (Linux support).\n\n## Notable wins\n\n- Subagent dispatch worked well — 5+10+3+2+3 parallel agents across waves with isolated worktrees and shared node_modules; only one stall (Wave 4 WS scope), which a slim re-dispatch resolved cleanly.\n- Cross-agent issues caught at the finalizer stage (registry wiring, YAML date coercion) rather than during agent dispatch — saves time vs. coordinating 10 agents on the same tweak.\n- The skill is now visible in this session's available-skills list — meta proof the loop closed.\n\n## Notable risks\n\n- Test-safety pattern (unsafe `os.homedir()` mocking) cost us once and could exist elsewhere — AW-9 captures the audit.\n- Package isn't on npm yet — install path untested end-to-end (AW-13)."
